Bundled dictionary / data attribution
-------------------------------------

The code in this repository is licensed under GPL-3.0. In addition, the
bundled dictionary and frequency data under `app/src/main/assets/tables/`
is generated from the following open data sources, each retaining its own
license obligations. Please keep these attributions when redistributing.

1) Standard (萬國蝦米) code table
   - Source: chinese-opendesktop/cin-tables, file `uniliu.cin` (萬國蝦米 / UniLiu)
     https://github.com/chinese-opendesktop/cin-tables
   - License: CC0-1.0  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
   - Used to build:
       * standard/dictionary.json  (97,030 entries)

2) Word list & character frequency statistics
   - Source: samejack/sc-dictionary
     https://github.com/samejack/sc-dictionary  (~1.1M words)
   - License: CC BY 3.0  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/
   - Used to build:
       * associations.json  (association / 聯想詞, 10k+ keys, 111k+ entries)
       * zhuyin/dictionary.json character frequencies (candidate ordering)

3) Character frequency table (standard/dictionary.json)
   - Source: 教育部語文司「常用字字頻表」表一，5,731 字原始出現頻次
     https://language.moe.gov.tw/001/Upload/files/SITE_CONTENT/M0001/BIAU1.zip
   - Counts are log-compressed to 1..999 so that user usage frequency
     (usageFrequency * 1000 in DictionaryManager) always outranks the
     static value, i.e. what you type once stays on top.
   - Used to build:
       * standard/dictionary.json character frequencies (candidate ordering)

4) Simplified character demotion
   - Source: OpenCC STCharacters.txt
     https://github.com/BYVoid/OpenCC
   - License: Apache-2.0  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
   - A character is demoted when OpenCC treats it as simplified and
     `s2t(char)` does not yield the character itself (so 谷 / 只 / 后 / 面 /
     板 keep their legitimate traditional readings).
   - Used to build:
       * zhuyin/dictionary.json  (frequency offset -1,000,000)
       * standard/dictionary.json (frequency offset -1,000,000)

Generation methodology notes are described in docs/ORIGINAL-TECH-PLAN.md and
tools/README.md. Regenerate the standard table with:

    python3 tools/build-dictionary.py

Redistribution of the bundled data must comply with CC BY 3.0 (attribution)
and Apache-2.0 requirements respectively.
